From 5958fc89d7b99cb9937745d0197cd215ff7ed573 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koshindai <97556702+Koshindai@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 11:18:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Launcher: eShop screenshots and icon in the artwork index

The artwork editor offers a game's eShop screenshots and icon besides its banner. The title list already names them, so
the index keeps them too (version 2), but only for the titles asked for: all of them would add some 10 MB to read at
every launch. A version 1 index is read again once, when the editor first asks, never at launch. A screenshot or the icon
is downloaded on request into artwork/<TITLEID>/, with the banners' checks (Nintendo's CDN only, at most 20 MB, an image
that decodes), and a slot that chose one shows it. One read of the list at a time.
